// I3C core register map (MIPI HCI 1.2), re-exported from the bender-vendored
// i3c-core fork so this IP's register collateral is generated like every other
// block's. Sibling of oca_i3c_wrap.rdl, the same way hw/ip/i2c/regs/ holds both
// i2c_wrap.rdl (the wrapper) and i2c.rdl (the core map it instantiates).
//
// oca_i3c_wrap also includes this same vendored registers.rdl and instantiates
// I3CCSR for the SMC address map. This entry is the standalone top used for
// field-level views -- gen/py/I3CCSR_reg.py for the cocotb TB under dv/tb,
// plus the C and address headers -- without the oca_i3c_wrap instance prefix.
//
// Two things this file must NOT do:
//   * wrap I3CCSR in another addrmap -- every generated symbol would gain an
//     instance prefix and stop matching the RTL/TB names;
//   * omit the vendor RDL dir from -I -- "registers.rdl" lives only under
//     i3c-core. OCAH_REG_EXTRA_SEARCH_* in hw/common/regs/classify.mk puts
//     that dir on this block's search path.

`include "registers.rdl"
